# What this machine says it is.
#
# **A machine that boots alo OS says Fedora on the way in.** GRUB offers
# "Fedora Linux 42 (Adams) (ostree:0)", systemd greets with "Welcome to Fedora
# Linux 42 (Adams)!", the login prompt reads "fedora login:", and the person
# standing at it has not installed Fedora.
#
# It is not only a name. The base's own `SUPPORT_END=2026-05-13` makes systemd
# print, in red, on every boot:
#
#     !! This OS version (Fedora Linux 42 (Adams)) is past its end-of-support
#        date (2026-05-13)
#
# **That is a support promise this project never made and cannot expire**, told
# to our own customer about our own product. Measured on a written disk,
# 2026-10-05.
#
# And it is a trademark matter rather than a preference. The Fedora Project asks
# that a modified remix not carry its marks, so shipping an image calling itself
# "Fedora Linux 42" is the wrong side of that line. Changing it is the correct
# thing, not a nicety.
#
# # What is kept, and why
#
# `ID_LIKE`, `VERSION_ID` and `PLATFORM_ID` stay Fedora's. Engines are
# configured, never patched: this image *is* built on Fedora 42, package tooling
# reasons about `$releasever` and the platform id, and a derivative that hides
# its base makes every later question about it harder to answer. The name a
# person reads changes; what the machine is built from is stated plainly.
#
# # Where this is applied
#
# `image/Containerfile` copies this over the base's own file **after the last
# `dnf`**, so no package resolution ever sees it. Nothing in this workspace
# reads `NAME` or `PRETTY_NAME`; the one reader is a walk's serial line, which
# prints whatever is here.
NAME="alo OS"
ID=alo
ID_LIKE=fedora
VERSION="0.0.6"
VERSION_ID=42
PRETTY_NAME="alo OS 0.0.6"
ANSI_COLOR="0;38;2;15;107;114"
CPE_NAME="cpe:/o:aloworld:alo_os:0.0.6"
PLATFORM_ID="platform:f42"
DEFAULT_HOSTNAME="alo"
HOME_URL="https://github.com/aloworld-org/alo-os"
DOCUMENTATION_URL="https://github.com/aloworld-org/alo-os/tree/main/docs"
SUPPORT_URL="https://github.com/aloworld-org/alo-os/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
BUG_REPORT_URL="https://github.com/aloworld-org/alo-os/issues"
